failNotRootT -- FP-N, SEQ 187 R2 (2026-10-04). A notifyFail rule ('fail') that is NOT the drive root fails past
offset 0: FnrOUT drives "(aQZ", its member FnrIN (flagged) matches "a" and fails at 2, where "QZ" starts. aCTionFailed
prints "Rule FnrIN" and "Failed at:" on STDOUT and then ENDS THE RUN (stopParsingInput), so nothing prints after it --
that is why FP-N has a file of its own and no sentinel line: the Failed-at line is the last output, by design.

The three readings, all measured 2026-10-04:
  trunk (seal 41)                      Failed at:  QZ                      -- its own point
  stroke12a as built (floor's point)   Failed at:  :reached end of input  -- the root has not failed yet, so empty
  stroke12a fixed (SEQ 187 R1)         Failed at:  QZ                      -- parse() hands aCTionFailed its own point
